\section*{Question 1}

Let \(R\) be the region enclosed by the graph of \(y=\sqrt{x-1}\), the vertical line \(x=10\), and the \(x\)-axis.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Find the area of \(R\).
\item[(b)] Find the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is revolved about the horizontal line \(y=3\).
\item[(c)] Find the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is revolved about the vertical line \(x=10\).
\item[(a)] Area \(=\int_{1}^{10} \sqrt{x-1} d x=18\)
(b)
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text { Volume } & =\pi \int_{1}^{10}\left(9-(3-\sqrt{x-1})^{2}\right) d x \\
& =212.057 \text { or } 212.058
\end{aligned}
\]
\end{itemize}
\[
3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}
1: \text { limits } \\
1: \text { integrand } \\
1: \text { answer }
\end{array}\right.
\]
